ediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWANO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A moving image display method which eliminates unnatural actions caused by discontinuous portions in the actions when a moving image is displayed with fewer frames, wherein a sequence of actions is divided into subdivisions (D1, D2) so that the first frames (D1S, D2S) and the last frames (D1E, D2E) in the individual subdivisions are not lost.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé d'affichage d'images mouvantes permettant d'éliminer les actions non naturelles qui sont dues à des parties discontinues des actions lorsqu'une image mouvante est affichée selon un nombre de trames moindre. Une séquence d'actions est divisée en sous-divisions (D1, D2) de sorte que les premières trames (D1S, D2S) et les dernières trames (D1E, D2E) des sous-divisions individuelles ne soient pas perdues.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>